# 1.00: Phase 1 - Buck Converter Objectives


## Project Introduction
The first phase of Project SLSB is learning the basics of DC-DC power conversion. 
I recently did a project on buck converters with the IEEE PES chapter at UT Dallas and learned a lot about power electronics (ie. buck converters) and simulation software used such as Simulink.
In this phase, I want to apply what I learned and using it for the output of a small solar panel, which I plan on researching the specs on.

First is learning LTspice as a simulation tool. 
Then I move to Simulink for more complex and variable behavior of the solar panel


## Objectives
# Create a working schematic of the buck converter for the solar panel in LTspice and Simulink through heavy simulation
# Use that schematic as a reference for the hardware to be built
